---
/**
 * The score-component control, and the thing it is careful not to claim.
 *
 * WHAT IT WOULD HAVE BOUND TO, AND WHY IT DOES NOT. The project's
 * reward-composition counterfactual reports that disabling one component of a
 * composed reward moves a quarter of the rollouts and reverses two thousand
 * signs. `design/scene/EVIDENCE-VERDICTS.md` §5 is binding here: that result
 * exists in two prose cells of a build record, its computation runs at test
 * time against a store outside both published repositories, and no per-rollout
 * before-and-after array ships anywhere. It may be stated with its limitation
 * and it may not become geometry or a control's displayed result.
 *
 * WHAT IT BINDS TO INSTEAD. The 200-step recorded run, which is complete and
 * per-trajectory, and this control states that record's own result. The result
 * is a negative and it is worth having: the run's score tree has exactly one
 * leaf, so there is nothing to redistribute. Turning the component off does not
 * shift the update toward another component, because there is no other
 * component; it removes the score from all 1,600 rollouts and leaves no
 * advantage defined at all.
 *
 * Every number below is computed at build time from
 * `src/data/scene/payload/*.bin`. Both summaries are in the document, so the
 * comparison is readable with scripting off and the control's effect on the
 * prose is a hidden attribute rather than a rewrite.
 */
import { scoreComponentFacts, group } from "./facts";

interface Props {
  class?: string;
}
const { class: extraClass = "" } = Astro.props;
const f = scoreComponentFacts();
const id = "scene-score-toggle";
const summaryId = "scene-score-summary";
---

<div class:list={["score", extraClass]}>
  <div class="score__control">
    <input
      type="checkbox"
      id={id}
      checked
      data-scene-score-toggle={f.leafName}
      aria-describedby={summaryId}
    />
    <label for={id} class="score__label">
      Score with <code>{f.leafName}</code>, this run's only reward component
    </label>
  </div>

  {/*
    The summary is the control's result and changing it is the reason the
    control exists, so it announces itself. It is one small region beside the
    control it belongs to, not a page-level live region: the only thing that
    ever speaks through it is this checkbox.
  */}
  <div class="score__summary" id={summaryId} aria-live="polite">
    <p class="type-body-sm" data-scene-score-summary="on">
      The score tree has {f.leafCount} leaf. {group(f.scoredRolloutCount)} of {group(f.rolloutCount)} recorded
      rollouts carry a value from it and on {group(f.abstainedRolloutCount)} the grader abstained. Of the
      advantages the estimator then computed, {group(f.reinforcedCount)} are positive, {group(f.discouragedCount)}
      are negative and {group(f.onAxisCount)} are exactly zero.
    </p>
    <p class="type-body-sm" data-scene-score-summary="off" hidden>
      With the only leaf removed there is no score on any of the {group(f.rolloutCount)} rollouts, so no group
      mean, no advantage and nothing reinforced. The count that changes is {group(f.scoredRolloutCount)} to 0.
      That is this run's whole answer to the question: a reward with one component cannot show how a
      reward divides between its components.
    </p>
    <p class="score__limit type-body-sm">
      A separate experiment reports that disabling one component of a composed reward moves about a
      quarter of the rollouts and reverses a few thousand signs. No per-rollout record of it ships with
      this site, so it is stated here and is not drawn, encoded or recomputed by this control.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .score {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .score__control {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: baseline;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .score__control input {
    accent-color: var(--control);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .score__control input:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--focus-width) solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: var(--focus-offset);
  }
  .score__label {
    color: var(--ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .score__label code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .score__summary {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    border-inline-start: var(--border-w-accent) solid var(--line-strong);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-4);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .score__summary p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .score__summary p[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .score__limit {
    color: var(--ink-3); /* ink3-ok: on --ground, 5.25:1 */
  }
</style>
